<h1>Hardware Settings - Sensor Tab</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description: Sensor</b></span> Tab changes options related to the sensor settings.</p>
<p><img src="../hw_sensor.gif" width="551px" height="485px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The tab is divided in four sections and a checkbox for 'Certified settings':</span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Profiles <a href="../../MMC/Settings/Profiles_in_HW_settings_(MMX,_MMZ,_MMC).htm"><img src="../../../../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></a></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><span style="text-decoration:none;">L</span>aser Power</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Click and drag the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Laser Power'</b></span> indicator to the desired setting or type-in the level in the box right to the slider. (1 is the minimum, 4 the maximum) The default value is 1.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><span style="text-decoration:none;">Ambient Threshold</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This box contains the ambient threshold setting of the current material item option. Sets the sensitivity of the sensor to surrounding light. A high value is used in a bright environment, a lower value in a darker environment. Lower values can be better at picking up darker colours. Default value is 96.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">MMIB</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Displays currently used MMIB type, Trigger ID and battery voltage.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Display warning when MMIB-DL battery low</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Check this option to enable message notification when MMIB-DL battery is low. Sometimes warning message about low battery voltage is randomly displayed even if the system is connected to main power supply. In this case it is recommended to disable this option.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Sets system triggering.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Best for localiser</b></span> option is checked then KUBE sets system triggering according to the current localiser that is installed. For FARO and CimCore localisers system triggering is disabled, for K-Scan it is enabled. If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Best for localiser</b></span> option is unchecked then user could manually select whether to use system triggering or not. It is strongly recommended to enable <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Best for localiser</b></span> option in order to use the proper triggering.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Sensor</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sensor type, Sensor serial number, Date of manufacture, and Temperature (internal temperature of the sensor) will be automatically detected by the software for Z sensors.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Sensor detection</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Auto</b></span> is selected then KUBE tries detecting all types of sensors until it finds the installed one. If set to <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Manual</b></span> then KUBE tries to detect only the sensor type, which is selected in the listbox. In case of fault it doesn't detect other types. Currently available options are 'MM X/Y', 'MM Z', 'MM D', and 'None'.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Refresh MMIB/Sensor status Button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This button is used to refresh the settings if a sensor is changed. This includes MMIB/sensor detection and loading the corresponding calibration file for the detected sensor.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Advanced Settings dialog</p>
<p class="whs6"><img src="../Z_Hardware_Sensor_Advanced_Settings.gif" width="531px" height="195px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Field of view</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Adjusts the stripe width of the sensor, giving more control over the data captured.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Wide'</b></span> uses full stripe width. Enabled by default.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Normal'</b></span> restricts the stripe width (varies for different sensors).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'Limit effective stripe'</b></span> checkbox to manually select the stripe width. Default value for stripe width is 20mm. Default value for Limit effective width is off.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Certified Settings checkbox</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When this option is enabled all settings in the tab are set to their default values. For the best results, it is recommended to use 'Certified settings'.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When all changes are made, confirm with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Apply'</b></span> button.</p>
